2026-09-26 follow-up — K01b: defined branch replacement and synchronization controls.

Correction to the historical MOV experiment below: Arm's concurrent-instruction
replacement guarantee covers specific instructions, including B/NOP, not arbitrary
MOV replacement. A later sync-core call does not authorize a reader racing that
MOV store. Therefore the old continuous-MOV results alone cannot establish an
architecture-defined emulator failure. They remain historical observations.
Arm's explanation and cited Arm ARM B2.2.5:
https://developer.arm.com/community/arm-community-blogs/b/architectures-and-processors-blog/posts/caches-self-modifying-code-working-with-threads

The corrected source uses one aligned direct B to immutable MOV/RET pairs.
It still publishes data before enabling, completes cache maintenance plus Linux
PRIVATE_EXPEDITED_SYNC_CORE after disabling, waits for read-side rwlock users,
then retires data. Readers need not stop while B is being replaced. Other modes
use an atomic memory gate with the SAME rwlock and syscall protocol, or hold
the write lock across MOV replacement. Handshake controls remain. Every
continuous mode must actually observe the enabled value; an idle reader cannot
produce PASS. GCC14/Clang19, O2/static/pthread, -Wall -Wextra -Werror, four CPUs,
512 rounds, 20 seconds each. No kernel patch, original test or lane change.

Six modes per compiler (12 programs), identical payload per flight:
                              GCC kernel         EvoCC kernel
MT TCG, Cortex-A72             6 PASS / 6 FAIL    6 PASS / 6 FAIL
HVF, host                    12 PASS / 0 FAIL   12 PASS / 0 FAIL
single-thread TCG, Cortex-A72 12 PASS / 0 FAIL   12 PASS / 0 FAIL
All 72 programs complete; all six boots/shutdowns PASS. The sealed native
container passes all 12. Only concurrent B replacement fails on MT-TCG:
                                         GCC kernel / EvoCC kernel misses
GCC single mapping                         964928 / 1189312
GCC aliases                               1170880 / 974208
GCC aliases plus ISB                        804736 / 641984
Clang single mapping                       585280 / 1050816
Clang aliases                              935552 / 1079680
Clang aliases plus ISB                      581824 / 1437440
Every first bad snapshot reads B encoding 14000001 (immutable return-zero
path), but the call returned 1 after data retirement. All memory-gate,
locked-MOV and handshake controls have zero misses on both kernels.
The first compile attempt had two -Werror signedness errors in this new
diagnostic; explicit result casts fix them. It is not a runtime RED or PASS.

This now isolates a shared concurrent instruction-publication failure with
architecture-appropriate instruction choices. It does not prove its exact QEMU
implementation cause or fix the original sched_ext crash. K01/K01b remain OPEN.
Versioned QEMU source suggests an invalidation/retranslation window worth
instrumenting: notdirty_write invalidates before the eventual store, while
tb_invalidate_phys_range_fast releases the page locks on return. This is a
source-based HYPOTHESIS, not a validated patch or permission to replace QEMU.
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qemu/qemu/v11.1.1/accel/tcg/cputlb.c
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qemu/qemu/v11.1.1/accel/tcg/tb-maint.c

